  "scope": "Authenticated multiplayer resource rallies for new Villagers and Fishing Ships, using the same production dispatcher as solo.",
  "behavior": {
    "authority": "Commands remain deferred until the authenticated host frame; full groups validate before any building rally is changed.",
    "targets": "Only live resource IDs currently visible to the issuing kingdom, still occupying their registered node cell, with matching resource coordinates. Farms/traps must belong to the issuing kingdom.",
    "compatibility": "Every producer must train the relevant worker kind. Ordinary ground rallies and original unit costs are preserved.",
    "production": "Uses unchanged applyProductionRally. A trained guest Villager gathers and delivers wood; a trained Fishing Ship inherits fish orders.",
    "persistence": "Existing save/load reconnects resource references to restored live nodes.",
    "protocol": "Existing bounded optional rally target field now admits resource IDs; packet version 2 and byte limits unchanged. Live channel/session v23 prevents mixed runtime peers; shell v187-resource-rally."
  },
